# AiVA Dashboard Design System Rules

This document captures how the current AiVA Dashboard implementation is wired so that Figma-driven updates (via the Model Context Protocol tools) can stay consistent with the codebase.

## Context Snapshot

- Primary mockups: [AiVA SaaS Dashboard Design](https://www.figma.com/make/IkF3MDpjCaZBohFOmgmri2/AiVA-SaaS-Dashboard-Design?node-id=0-1&t=GHbiYV5YToi0SwTM-1)
- React-based reference build lives in `docs/design/code/AiVA SaaS Dashboard Design` and should be consulted whenever the Vue app needs fidelity updates.

```3:15:docs/design/code/README.md
This directory contains the **AiVA SaaS Dashboard Design** - a React-based clickable prototype that serves as a reference for frontend implementation.
```

---

## 1. Token Definitions

**Location & format**

- All design tokens are CSS custom properties defined once in `resources/css/app.css`. They were ported from the design system’s `globals.css` and are injected globally because `app.ts` imports the stylesheet before Vue mounts.
- Token categories include typography, color system, spacing/radii, glassmorphism presets, and background layers.

```7:100:resources/css/app.css
:root {
    --font-size: 16px;
    --typography-header-size: 16px;
    --typography-metrics-weight: 600;
    --color-text-primary: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    --color-accent-positive: #4ef081;
    --color-glass-fill: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    /* ...additional tokens for badges, cards, shadows, and backgrounds... */
}
```

**Usage guidelines**

- Prefer CSS variables for anything that maps 1:1 with Figma tokens (colors, typography, radii) and layer Tailwind utilities for layout.
- Tailwind v4 is used without theme extensions (`tailwind.config.js`). If a new Figma token needs Tailwind utility access, either rely on `var(--token-name)` directly or extend Tailwind’s theme once.
- There is no token build/transform pipeline yet—any updates must be edited manually in `app.css`.

