## 2. Component Library

**Structure**

- Shared primitives live in `resources/js/components`, while route-level UIs stay under `resources/js/pages`.
- Every component is a Vue 3 Single File Component using `<script setup lang="ts">` with Pinia stores for state.
- Navigation, forms, and tables are implemented directly in the page components; there is no Storybook or doc site.

```38:74:resources/js/components/admin/AdminNav.vue
<nav class="bg-white shadow-sm border-b border-gray-200 mb-6" aria-label="Superadmin navigation">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 py-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 sm:gap-8">
                <router-link v-for="link in navLinks" :key="link.name" :to="{ name: link.name }">
                    <!-- ... -->
```

**Implementation notes**

- Reusable logic belongs in Pinia stores under `resources/js/stores`. Components read from stores during `setup()`; keep asynchronous fetching out of templates to avoid inconsistent hydration.
- When porting React reference components, match the structure under `resources/js/pages/...` to keep router lazy-loading intact.

