## 4. Asset Management

- Laravel’s Blade entrypoint (`resources/views/app.blade.php`) uses `@vite` to load the compiled app, so any new assets bundled by Vite (fonts, images) must be imported from Vue/TS code.
- Static files that should bypass bundling belong in `public/`; Vite copies hashed assets referenced via `import`.
- No CDN configuration is present; assets are served by Laravel directly. Optimization relies on Vite’s default Rollup minification and manifest splitting.

```1:12:resources/views/app.blade.php
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ str_replace('_', '-', app()->getLocale()) }}">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    @vite(['resources/js/app.ts'])
</head>
<body>
    <div id="app"></div>
</body>
</html>
```

