## 5. Icon System

- There is no shared icon library yet. Components inline raw SVG paths (Heroicons-inspired) and tint them with `currentColor`.
- When importing Figma icons, convert them to inline SVGs or create a dedicated icon component folder so the same pattern can be reused.

```2:23:resources/js/components/TenantSwitcher.vue
<button class="flex items-center space-x-2 px-4 py-2 ...">
    <span>{{ currentTenantName }}</span>
    <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
    </svg>
</button>
```

**Naming guidance**

- Follow `PascalCase` when creating new icon components (e.g., `ChevronDownIcon.vue`) and drop them in `resources/js/components/icons` once created. Reference them via `<ChevronDownIcon class="w-4 h-4 text-gray-500" />` to keep color control external.

