## 6. Styling Approach

- Tailwind utility classes drive layout, spacing, and typographic scale; CSS variables handle theme values.
- Global resets (html/body sizing) and root tokens load via `resources/css/app.css`.
- Responsive behavior leverages Tailwind breakpoints (`sm:`, `lg:`) directly inside Vue templates, matching how the React reference uses `@media`.

```2:58:resources/js/pages/admin/auth/LoginPage.vue
<div class="min-h-screen flex items-center justify-center bg-gray-50 py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-md w-full space-y-8">
        <h2 class="mt-6 text-center text-3xl font-extrabold text-gray-900">
            Superadmin Login
        </h2>
        <!-- ... -->
        <button
            class="group relative w-full flex justify-center py-2 px-4 ... focus:ring-indigo-500 focus:ring-offset-2"
        >
            <!-- ... -->
        </button>
    </div>
</div>
```

**Responsive playbook**

- Figma’s mobile/desktop breakpoints map directly to Tailwind’s `sm`/`lg`. Use CSS tokens for consistent padding/radius so glassmorphism depth stays aligned with the prototype.
- For glass panels, compose `background-color: var(--glassfx-v2-fill)` and `border: var(--glassfx-v2-border)` inside either a component-level `<style scoped>` block or inline `style` bindings if a utility is unavailable.

