## MCP + Figma Integration Workflow

1. **Inspect design references**  
   - Use the provided Figma link to grab node IDs for the relevant screen.  
   - Optionally, run the React prototype in `docs/design/code/AiVA SaaS Dashboard Design` to see responsive interactions before translating them into Vue.

2. **Pull structured context via MCP**  
   - `mcp_Figma_get_design_context` is the preferred tool; pass the `nodeId` from the Figma URL plus the file key extracted from the same link. Request assets if you need downloadable icons or illustrations.
   - If you need variable definitions (colors, spacing) straight from Figma, call `mcp_Figma_get_variable_defs` for the node to compare against the CSS tokens above.

3. **Map tokens to implementation**  
   - Colors/typography → `resources/css/app.css` variables.  
   - Spacing/radii → Tailwind utilities first; fall back to CSS variables if the design uses non-standard values.  
   - Component structure → mirror the hierarchy outlined in `README-FRONTEND.md` so router-based code splitting stays stable.

4. **Reconcile assets/icons**  
   - Export icons via MCP (or copy SVG source) and add them as inline Vue components; follow the naming convention described in section 5.

5. **Document deviations**  
   - If Figma introduces a new token that cannot be expressed today, append it to the `:root` block and update this rules file with the mapping so future MCP calls remain aware of the new token.

---

## Quick Checklist for New UI Work

- [ ] Confirm the target Figma node and grab measurements/assets via MCP.
- [ ] Update or add CSS tokens in `resources/css/app.css` when new semantic values are introduced.
- [ ] Keep new shared UI in `resources/js/components`; reserve `resources/js/pages` for router-level views.
- [ ] Use Tailwind utilities plus `var(--token)` values to stay faithful to GlassFX styling.
- [ ] Inline SVG icons or create dedicated icon components—no external icon font usage yet.
- [ ] Run `npm run build && php artisan test` (or relevant frontend tests) before shipping to ensure Vite manifest and routers remain healthy.
